WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:54.900 --> 00:00:55.760
- Hi everyone.

00:00:55.760 --> 00:00:59.323
Welcome to our daily live stream.

00:01:00.230 --> 00:01:01.400
This is why we've almost,

00:01:01.400 --> 00:01:03.290
we've been doing this for a
little bit over two weeks.

00:01:03.290 --> 00:01:05.550
For those of you all who are new to this,

00:01:05.550 --> 00:01:07.880
the whole point of this is Khan Academy

00:01:07.880 --> 00:01:09.860
is a not-for-profit, with
a mission of providing

00:01:09.860 --> 00:01:12.480
a free world-class education
for anyone anywhere.

00:01:12.480 --> 00:01:14.900
And over the last many years,

00:01:14.900 --> 00:01:18.170
we've been building
resources that start in pre-K

00:01:18.170 --> 00:01:20.940
with Khan Academy kids through elementary,

00:01:20.940 --> 00:01:24.330
middle, high school and the
core of college, not just math,

00:01:24.330 --> 00:01:27.230
not just videos, but deep
interactive exercises,

00:01:27.230 --> 00:01:29.790
dashboards for teachers,
English and language arts,

00:01:29.790 --> 00:01:33.760
history, sciences, SAT preparation.

00:01:33.760 --> 00:01:37.420
And, that has made us very well-suited

00:01:37.420 --> 00:01:41.140
to really step up for
the country and the world

00:01:41.140 --> 00:01:43.370
as we go through these school closures.

00:01:43.370 --> 00:01:44.720
But we realize we need to do

00:01:44.720 --> 00:01:47.470
as much as possible on top of that.

00:01:47.470 --> 00:01:49.320
And so the whole point of this live stream

00:01:49.320 --> 00:01:52.170
is for all of you who
are using Khan Academy

00:01:52.170 --> 00:01:53.730
or thinking about using Khan Academy

00:01:53.730 --> 00:01:56.620
or just trying to navigate
the school closures generally.

00:01:56.620 --> 00:02:00.210
We wanted a place for folks to
connect, and feel connected,

00:02:00.210 --> 00:02:03.740
especially in this time
of social distancing.

00:02:03.740 --> 00:02:05.953
And so, every day it's very informal.

00:02:05.953 --> 00:02:08.510
Myself and I gonna bring
some team members on,

00:02:08.510 --> 00:02:09.970
we sometimes have special guests,

00:02:09.970 --> 00:02:11.540
we try to answer your questions

00:02:11.540 --> 00:02:14.330
and I make any announcements
that are relevant.

00:02:14.330 --> 00:02:16.560
I do wanna start off
with reminding everyone

00:02:16.560 --> 00:02:17.520
we are not-for-profit,

00:02:17.520 --> 00:02:19.450
we are funded by philanthropic support

00:02:19.450 --> 00:02:20.820
from folks like yourself.

00:02:20.820 --> 00:02:23.160
We were running at a deficit
that even before this crisis

00:02:23.160 --> 00:02:26.100
and with this crisis
our server load is up,

00:02:26.100 --> 00:02:28.710
is roughly 250% of what it normally is,

00:02:28.710 --> 00:02:31.460
our registrations are six x from teachers

00:02:31.460 --> 00:02:32.880
and parents of what it normally is.

00:02:32.880 --> 00:02:34.730
Parent registrations are 20x.

00:02:34.730 --> 00:02:36.420
So if any of you find
yourself in a position

00:02:36.420 --> 00:02:39.420
that you can donate, please
think about doing so.

00:02:39.420 --> 00:02:41.110
I wanna give a special shout out

00:02:41.110 --> 00:02:43.000
to several corporations who've stepped up

00:02:43.000 --> 00:02:46.530
in the last few weeks with
very short notice to help us,

00:02:46.530 --> 00:02:47.940
although we need more help.

00:02:47.940 --> 00:02:50.900
Bank of America was the
first followed by 18T,

00:02:50.900 --> 00:02:53.640
google.org and Novartis
but we need more help

00:02:53.640 --> 00:02:55.623
from individuals and corporations.

00:02:55.623 --> 00:02:57.993
We are literally going to go millions,

00:03:01.750 --> 00:03:04.160
few weeks and months.

00:03:04.160 --> 00:03:06.630
But with that said, I would love to,

00:03:06.630 --> 00:03:09.760
I'll bring my colleague
Dan on who helps me

00:03:09.760 --> 00:03:13.180
answer all of the questions
that we get on the live stream,

00:03:13.180 --> 00:03:15.900
and I encourage all of you
all to start asking questions

00:03:15.900 --> 00:03:18.050
on whatever you're using, YouTube,

00:03:18.050 --> 00:03:19.870
Facebook, whatever channel.

00:03:19.870 --> 00:03:21.670
And, let's see,

00:03:21.670 --> 00:03:23.490
it seems like there's already
a couple of questions,

00:03:23.490 --> 00:03:26.460
but then you can always
jump in, but this question,

00:03:26.460 --> 00:03:31.020
it's from YouTube, this
is Crazy Cookie 3,908.

00:03:31.020 --> 00:03:31.890
It's pretty impressive

00:03:31.890 --> 00:03:36.160
that there were probably 3,973 before you.

00:03:38.000 --> 00:03:40.450
Hey Sal, will there be summer classes?

00:03:40.450 --> 00:03:43.310
Will this be all-year round?

00:03:43.310 --> 00:03:46.540
That's actually a super powerful question,

00:03:46.540 --> 00:03:48.863
Crazy Cookie 3,908.

00:03:51.110 --> 00:03:52.710
You know, I think about two weeks ago,

00:03:52.710 --> 00:03:55.250
the school closures were
announced in this country

00:03:55.250 --> 00:03:56.607
and really through the world,

00:03:56.607 --> 00:03:59.210
there's 50 million students
out of school in just the US

00:03:59.210 --> 00:04:01.910
pretty much close to a billion globally,

00:04:01.910 --> 00:04:03.930
and it happened so fast

00:04:03.930 --> 00:04:07.880
because of just the health emergency.

00:04:07.880 --> 00:04:11.970
And I don't think a lot of
thought was no one had time

00:04:11.970 --> 00:04:13.350
to think about what the implications

00:04:13.350 --> 00:04:15.980
but now it's becoming clear
that in most of the world,

00:04:15.980 --> 00:04:18.480
the school closures actually might happen

00:04:18.480 --> 00:04:19.820
through the summer.

00:04:19.820 --> 00:04:23.050
And so, the way we've
been thinking about this,

00:04:23.050 --> 00:04:25.490
we wanna be able to support teachers,

00:04:25.490 --> 00:04:28.040
parents, students over the next two months

00:04:28.040 --> 00:04:29.990
so that we can keep
the learning happening,

00:04:29.990 --> 00:04:33.100
keep everyone learning,
but we also see summer

00:04:33.100 --> 00:04:36.760
as a really powerful
opportunity to keep going.

00:04:36.760 --> 00:04:40.320
There's no reason that once
you've built the practices

00:04:40.320 --> 00:04:41.680
and the habits to keep learning

00:04:41.680 --> 00:04:43.900
over what would be the
traditional school year,

00:04:43.900 --> 00:04:45.380
that whether you're a
student, parent or teacher,

00:04:45.380 --> 00:04:48.020
that you can't go over
those three months as well.

00:04:48.020 --> 00:04:50.160
And that might be the silver lining of,

00:04:50.160 --> 00:04:52.300
historically summer has been, you know,

00:04:52.300 --> 00:04:53.570
there's the term summer slide,

00:04:53.570 --> 00:04:56.170
it's been a time for a lost learning

00:04:56.170 --> 00:04:59.313
and now we have an opportunity to do,

00:05:00.290 --> 00:05:03.189
now we have an opportunity
to make it a valuable

00:05:03.189 --> 00:05:04.740
for learning purposes.

00:05:04.740 --> 00:05:08.270
And so, yes, simple answer
what we're trying to do

00:05:08.270 --> 00:05:10.390
in response to the school
closures and COVID,

00:05:10.390 --> 00:05:12.820
we expect to be able to
do through the summer.

00:05:12.820 --> 00:05:15.780
And I think next school year
is going to be interesting.

00:05:15.780 --> 00:05:18.220
We all hope that the social distancing,

00:05:18.220 --> 00:05:22.220
the school closures are not
in place as of back to school.

00:05:22.220 --> 00:05:23.630
Hopefully the summer temperatures

00:05:23.630 --> 00:05:26.720
will help kill some of that
virus, reduce the spread

00:05:26.720 --> 00:05:28.820
but there is a possibility

00:05:28.820 --> 00:05:30.810
that in October, November, December,

00:05:30.810 --> 00:05:32.710
what's traditionally flu season

00:05:32.710 --> 00:05:35.440
could actually make COVID go up again.

00:05:35.440 --> 00:05:38.740
And so we also wanna think
about if that happens,

00:05:38.740 --> 00:05:40.260
how we can continue to support folks.

00:05:40.260 --> 00:05:44.210
But, the big takeaway is
summer is an opportunity

00:05:44.210 --> 00:05:47.660
that we all have to
keep everyone learning.

00:05:47.660 --> 00:05:49.484
Excellent question.

00:05:49.484 --> 00:05:50.630
All right.

00:05:50.630 --> 00:05:52.860
So there's a another question.

00:05:52.860 --> 00:05:53.850
This is from Facebook.

00:05:53.850 --> 00:05:57.420
Dina Everett Nevos says, hi,
I'm apparent and new to Khan,

00:05:57.420 --> 00:05:58.979
I saw the sample daily agendas.

00:05:58.979 --> 00:06:03.090
How do I link the daily schedule
to my children's accounts?

00:06:03.090 --> 00:06:04.200
Thanks.

00:06:04.200 --> 00:06:08.270
Well, Dina, the schedules
are very simple documents

00:06:08.270 --> 00:06:10.480
and you can actually adapt them,
you can copy and paste them

00:06:10.480 --> 00:06:13.180
into your own docs and
adapt them as necessary.

00:06:13.180 --> 00:06:15.400
And those just have links

00:06:15.400 --> 00:06:18.590
to the relevant part of Khan Academy.

00:06:18.590 --> 00:06:23.440
And what if the student, if
your child clicks on the link,

00:06:23.440 --> 00:06:26.820
it will go to their Khan Academy
and if they are logged in,

00:06:26.820 --> 00:06:28.560
they will show up as a logged in users.

00:06:28.560 --> 00:06:32.020
So, if they click from their computers

00:06:32.020 --> 00:06:34.680
or whatever they're using, if
they click on that, you know,

00:06:34.680 --> 00:06:37.660
let's call it fifth grade
English and language arts

00:06:37.660 --> 00:06:40.190
on that document, they'll
go to Khan Academy

00:06:40.190 --> 00:06:42.030
and see fifth grade language arts,

00:06:42.030 --> 00:06:43.930
and if they're not logged
in, they can log in

00:06:43.930 --> 00:06:45.480
and there'll be logged into
fifth grade language arts.

00:06:45.480 --> 00:06:47.730
And if they're already
logged in on that computer,

00:06:47.730 --> 00:06:50.220
they will be on their accounts.

00:06:50.220 --> 00:06:51.970
So I think that's what
you might be asking.

00:06:51.970 --> 00:06:54.300
And that brings up another
interesting thing is, you know,

00:06:54.300 --> 00:06:55.480
we've made those schedules,

00:06:55.480 --> 00:06:57.390
we made four different versions of them.

00:06:57.390 --> 00:07:00.680
One for kind of the pre-K
kindergarten first grade crowd,

00:07:00.680 --> 00:07:02.620
one for the elementary crowd,

00:07:02.620 --> 00:07:04.487
and then one for the middle school

00:07:04.487 --> 00:07:06.610
and one for the late high school crowd.

00:07:06.610 --> 00:07:09.630
And what you could do is then make them

00:07:09.630 --> 00:07:12.070
even more fine tuned for
your children's needs.

00:07:12.070 --> 00:07:15.630
Because for example, for the
late elementary crowd, we said,

00:07:15.630 --> 00:07:17.420
okay, you might wanna use third grade

00:07:17.420 --> 00:07:18.700
or fourth grade or fifth
grade or sixth grade

00:07:18.700 --> 00:07:21.410
or seventh grade math on Khan Academy

00:07:21.410 --> 00:07:23.940
and depending on the
strength of the student,

00:07:23.940 --> 00:07:25.680
you might wanna remediate it or not

00:07:25.680 --> 00:07:27.360
but you know all your
children better than anyone

00:07:27.360 --> 00:07:28.640
and they know themselves hopefully.

00:07:28.640 --> 00:07:30.250
And so you can narrow that down, you know,

00:07:30.250 --> 00:07:33.540
work on sixth grade or if you
had some weak foundations,

00:07:33.540 --> 00:07:35.250
work on fourth and fifth grade

00:07:35.250 --> 00:07:36.700
while you work on sixth grade as well.

00:07:36.700 --> 00:07:39.610
So I completely encourage you to fine tune

00:07:39.610 --> 00:07:41.963
those schedules for your children's needs.

00:07:42.860 --> 00:07:44.250
- So Sal, I would add next week

00:07:44.250 --> 00:07:47.220
we are hosting some parent
webinars for different age groups

00:07:47.220 --> 00:07:50.360
specifically and we'll be
