00:08:12.850 --> 00:08:15.350
can you post something on
Khan Academy about that?

00:08:16.590 --> 00:08:19.560
- So Arov, we want to help you.

00:08:19.560 --> 00:08:22.790
We currently do not
have what you could call

00:08:22.790 --> 00:08:25.780
fourth-grade science on Khan Academy,

00:08:25.780 --> 00:08:29.240
but we, and I hope over
time we are able to add that

00:08:29.240 --> 00:08:30.830
and I'll remind everyone
we're not-for-profit.

00:08:30.830 --> 00:08:32.010
The more support we get,

00:08:32.010 --> 00:08:34.470
the more we can think
about adding more subjects.

00:08:34.470 --> 00:08:38.770
But, if you are genuinely
interested in science,

00:08:38.770 --> 00:08:40.570
I think there are places you can start.

00:08:40.570 --> 00:08:43.560
I actually think that you could,

00:08:43.560 --> 00:08:48.090
we have several, for example,
even our high school biology,

00:08:48.090 --> 00:08:50.610
I know you're only, I'm
guessing nine years old,

00:08:50.610 --> 00:08:52.330
and high school biology
could seem daunting,

00:08:52.330 --> 00:08:54.100
but I actually think
some of the intro levels

00:08:54.100 --> 00:08:56.960
of high school biology
you could start to engage

00:08:56.960 --> 00:08:59.660
in my oldest son is about,

00:08:59.660 --> 00:09:01.696
is actually a little bit older than you,

00:09:01.696 --> 00:09:02.529
my daughter is about your age.

00:09:02.529 --> 00:09:03.550
And actually I've been doing stuff

00:09:03.550 --> 00:09:05.110
even in some of the early chemistry,

00:09:05.110 --> 00:09:07.550
high school chemistry units
on, what's an element,

00:09:07.550 --> 00:09:09.490
what's an atom, what's an atomic number?

00:09:09.490 --> 00:09:10.530
I think these are types of things

00:09:10.530 --> 00:09:11.980
