00:10:17.550 --> 00:10:20.550
So, from YouTube, Steven Amenzo says,

00:10:20.550 --> 00:10:22.590
when was Khan Academy founded?

00:10:22.590 --> 00:10:26.000
And Steven, if you do a web
search, you'll find a lot of,

00:10:26.000 --> 00:10:29.338
you know, talks on
YouTube and other places

00:10:29.338 --> 00:10:31.710
for me talking about that.

00:10:31.710 --> 00:10:32.690
So if you want it in depth,

00:10:32.690 --> 00:10:34.460
I recommend you you're doing that

00:10:34.460 --> 00:10:39.460
but long story short, about
14, 50, actually 16 years ago.

00:10:39.720 --> 00:10:40.615
I'm getting old.

00:10:40.615 --> 00:10:43.630
My cousin Nadia, who was 12 at the time

00:10:43.630 --> 00:10:46.430
needed help with math and I
started tutoring her remotely.

00:10:46.430 --> 00:10:48.949
Worked around my family that
free tutoring was going on,

00:10:48.949 --> 00:10:52.670
and so people, and so I
started making resources

00:10:52.670 --> 00:10:53.769
to scale it up.

00:10:53.769 --> 00:10:55.400
At first it had nothing to do with videos.

00:10:55.400 --> 00:10:56.930
I was creating the software part,

00:10:56.930 --> 00:10:59.300
the early version of what you
can now the practice software

00:10:59.300 --> 00:11:01.370
in Khan Academy and
then a friend suggested

00:11:01.370 --> 00:11:02.800
that I make videos to supplement it

00:11:02.800 --> 00:11:05.350
and that kind of took on
a life of its own in 2009.

00:11:07.660 --> 00:11:09.440
2008 I set it up as a not-for-profit,

00:11:09.440 --> 00:11:11.240
which just means no one owns Khan Academy.

00:11:11.240 --> 00:11:13.770
I don't own Khan Academy, I'm
an employee of Khan Academy,

00:11:13.770 --> 00:11:16.020
I own as much as you own of Khan Academy,

00:11:16.020 --> 00:11:19.510
and then 2009 was when I quit my day job

00:11:19.510 --> 00:11:21.510
to try to work on this full-time.

00:11:21.510 --> 00:11:22.449
It was a tough year.

00:11:22.449 --> 00:11:23.282
(laughs)

00:11:23.282 --> 00:11:24.560
I was living off of savings,

00:11:24.560 --> 00:11:27.370
but then in 2010 we got
some of our first support

00:11:27.370 --> 00:11:29.120
from some foundations and corporations.

00:11:29.120 --> 00:11:32.490
And so we've been able to
grow all the way till today

00:11:32.490 --> 00:11:35.410
where we're over 200 folks, we
have thousands of volunteers,

00:11:35.410 --> 00:11:37.180
there's 40 translation efforts

00:11:37.180 --> 00:11:38.560
around the world of Khan Academy,

00:11:38.560 --> 00:11:40.450
we're trying to add subjects and grades

00:11:40.450 --> 00:11:43.860
and we were already reaching
17, 18, 19 million students

00:11:43.860 --> 00:11:45.540
a month before the crisis and it looks

00:11:45.540 --> 00:11:49.440
like our daily users is up roughly 50% now

00:11:49.440 --> 00:11:52.148
and our actual total traffic is up 2.5.

00:11:52.148 --> 00:11:54.730
And so it's been a bit of a wild ride

00:11:54.730 --> 00:11:57.500
but we feel privileged
to be able to support you

00:11:57.500 --> 00:11:59.650
and so many other folks.

